Let me share a recent challenging project I worked on.

In my current role, I led the migration of an on-premise data pipeline to a cloud-native solution using PySpark, Hive,
and Impala on a Hadoop ecosystem.
The challenge was to deliver transformation and extrapolation for large number of files which is time consuming.
I came up with approach to make it configurable and have flexible, reusable solution.
It took time to code and unit test the same initially, but it helps to deliver things faster at last.

It requires transformation logic revamp, metadata management, and coordination across multiple teams.

The project required taking raw CSV files, transforming them through multiple stages — Lake ➝ Hub ➝ Mart,
ensuring data consistency, partitioning, performance optimization, and proper lineage tracking.

One major roadblock was inconsistent schema evolution, especially with third-party feeds.
these configurable setup helped to overcome this bottleneck too without breaking the pipelines.

We also had to make the deployment seamless across environments,
so I set up configurable workflow for database migrations and Dockerized the setup to make it reproducible and CI/CD friendly.

This project taught me how to balance agility with robustness and highlighted the importance of clear documentation,
automation, and observability in data engineering.